{
  "dom_id": "step-q109354",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "The probability distributions of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{5}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{5}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{5}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{8}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{8}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFind $\\text{E}[XY].$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+6\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+9\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}=7 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+6\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}=\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]=7\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}=\\frac{63}{2}.\n$$",
